==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
[[pun|Pun]] on the pronunciation of "I seek you."

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ī"sē-kyū'}}, {{IPA|en|/ˌaɪsiːˈkjuː/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ICQ.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|ham radio}} A call for acknowledgement.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|Internet}} A program allowing users to send each other [[instant message]]s via the [[Internet]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Laura Lambert|author2=Chris Woodford|author3=Christos J. P. Moschovitis|title=The Internet: A Historical Encyclopedia|publisher=ABC-CLIO|isbn=9781851096596|page=136|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=qi-ItIG6QLwC&pg=RA2-PA136&dq=%22ICQ%22&hl=es&cd=2&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22ICQ%22&f=false|text='''ICQ''' was unusual among instant-messaging systems because it used what is called peer-to-peer technology—'''ICQ''' users essentially communicated with each other directly, without having all their messages pass through a central server.}}

